<title>NETHERLANDS: Fortis AG mulls rights issue - Fortis.</title>
<headline>Fortis AG mulls rights issue - Fortis.</headline>
<dateline>UTRECHT, Netherlands 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch-Belgian financial group Fortis said on Friday that its 50 percent shareholder Fortis AG was considering a rights issue to help fund the group's acquisition of investment bank MeesPierson.  </p>
<p>Fortis earlier announced it had sealed the purchase of the investment bank from ABN AMRO for 2.5 billion guilders.</p>
<p>&quot;They (Fortis' parent companies) will share the costs and AG is considering a (rights) issue. A decision could be taken in January,&quot; Fortis group spokeswoman Saskia van Opijnen told Reuters.</p>
<p>Fortis group said in a statement that Fortis Amev would pay for its share of the costs from its own resources.</p>
<p>Fortis earlier said the buy, first signalled on October 4, would make a positive contribution to earnings per share over 1997.</p>
